  "description": "Pure-managed JPEG (ITU-T T.81 / ISO 10918) codec for .NET. Decoder: baseline sequential + progressive DCT, restart intervals, 4:4:4 / 4:2:2 / 4:2:0 / arbitrary chroma subsampling, grayscale, YCbCr, RGB-marked, and Adobe CMYK / YCCK (APP14) streams, plus scaled decode at 1/2, 1/4, 1/8 resolution via reduced inverse DCT — a 33-megapixel source can decode straight to a thumbnail-sized raster without the full-resolution intermediate ever existing. Encoder: baseline sequential (Annex K or per-image optimised Huffman tables) or progressive DCT, YCbCr 4:4:4 / 4:2:0 or single-component grey, quality 1..100, with Vector256 / Vector128 / scalar colour conversion and forward DCT that give identical output on every ISA; at the same quality it matches or beats libjpeg-turbo on luma PSNR and size. Decodes MCU row by MCU row straight into the caller's buffer (RGBA / BGRA / RGB at any stride) with no managed allocation and a working set of a few MCU rows, with Vector256 / Vector128 (SSE, AdvSimd) / scalar kernels that are bit-identical across ISAs; JpegSegmentScanner surfaces APPn metadata segments. Entropy decoding is coefficient-exact against libjpeg-turbo; sample reconstruction (single-precision IDCT, unrounded chroma interpolation, T.871 colour conversion) is at least as close to a double-precision reference as libjpeg-turbo's accurate mode. AOT-compatible.",
